content Analyze buy gap protection and decay function effectiveness.
	
	## Goal
	Optimize the buy gap protection that prevents accumulating lots at similar prices.
	
	## Current Logic (main.go:381-434)
	- Only buy if price dropped enough from last buy (ratchet prevention)
	- Gap scales up with inventory (doubles at 100% target)
	- Decay over time after sells: decay = exp(-timeRatio * periodScale)
	- Base decay period is 30s, scaled by inventory ratio
	
	## Analysis
	- Effectiveness of gap protection (prevented bad buys?)
	- Decay function comparison (exponential vs linear)
	- Optimal decay period (currently 30s)
	- Inventory scaling factor optimization
	
	## Experiments
	- Test buygap = {3, 5, 7, 10} bps
	- Test decay = {15s, 30s, 60s, 120s}
	- Measure gap hit rate (how often does gap prevent buys?)
